cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use splitkit in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "splitkit: leakage-free, class-balanced splits of grouped data"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kuźniar"
    given-names: "Marcin"
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MarcinKvzniar/splitkit"
abstract: >-
  splitkit splits grouped datasets (several images per patient, tiles per slide)
  into train, validation and test sets without group leakage, while matching the
  class distribution in every split. It treats the split as an optimisation
  problem and solves it with simulated annealing, differential evolution, or exact
  mixed-integer programming.
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - data splitting
  - stratification
  - group leakage
  - medical imaging
